  "scope_notes": "Modifies shared RPC argument parsing mechanisms (alias type resolution, OpenRPC schemas, and named argument transformation) in addition to walletprocesspsbt itself.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Converts walletprocesspsbt to take an options dictionary as its second argument while preserving backwards compatibility for callers using the legacy positional boolean and string parameters. Today, walletprocesspsbt requires up to four trailing positional parameters, making invocations unwieldy and requiring any new functionality (such as in PR 32857) to append yet another positional parameter. The change also enhances the core RPC framework to support distinct types per parameter alias and updates OpenRPC schema generation. Unblocks adding new settings cleanly to walletprocesspsbt without growing the positional argument list.",
